  "id": "rationnine",
  "neon": "#ffb43a",
  "note": "RATION NINE — the municipal ration store on the east side of Ironside Street.\n\n⚠ THE QUEUE IS THE BUILDING. Everything a ration store does happens on the pavement outside it, so\nthe composition is a long canopy on posts with shutters behind it and almost nothing else: one hall,\none awning, two hatches and a number. A shopfront would be wrong — there is nothing to display and\nnobody is browsing.\n\n⚠ AND THE NUMBER IS BIGGER THAN THE NAME. Nine is what people call it and NINE is what is painted on\nit; the full name is the small lettering underneath, the way a municipal building actually signs\nitself. That is also why the hand is stencil and the palette is olive rather than anything a shop\nwould choose: this is issued, not sold.\n\n⚠ IT REPLACES ITS OWN ARM RATHER THAN STANDING BESIDE IT. `rationnine` is a NAMED arm drawing this\none tile, so the bind key and the arm key are the same and `replaces` is a true statement about the\nrevert path as well as about the trade — `LEGACY_MODELS` holds the arm and `RENDER_TUNE.legacyArms`\nputs it back. A file that merely bound by name would lose to it (the registry merge is `??=`).",
  "pal": "ty_fallow",
  "replaces": "rationnine",
